     "blocks": [
      {
       "t": "prose",
       "md": "The model behind [Minimum Wage with Heterogeneous Workers](note:minimum-wage-with-heterogeneous-workers). Place that view, not this note."
      },
      {
       "t": "prose",
       "md": "- **Model.** The lecture's Theory III ([Minimum Wage](note:minimum-wage)): worker $i$ produces $A_i$ and is paid $\\beta p A_i$; with a floor, an employed worker earns $\\max\\{\\beta p A_i, w_{mw}\\}$ and is hired only if $pA_i \\ge w_{mw}$. Abilities are uniform between $A_{min}$ and $A_{max}$ so that shares can be read off.\n- **Tests.** Python."
      }
     ],
